<main><section class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / DATA ENGINEERING · RELIABILITY LAB</p><h1>Break the pipeline.<br><span>Keep the truth.</span></h1><div class="intro-bottom"><p>Orders repeat. Workers crash. Bad records arrive.<br>SignalWorks makes recovery visible—and verifiable.</p><a class="cta" href="#lab">Explore the lab ↘</a></div><div class="byline">BY KARTIKEYA RANA <span>PYTHON / SQL / SQLITE / ANATOMY SVG</span></div></section>
<section id="lab" aria-labelledby="lab-title"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / INTERACTIVE EXPERIMENT</p><h2 id="lab-title">A little machine.<br>A real failure mode.</h2></div><p id="disclosure">Interactive replay of a recorded local run using synthetic data.</p></div>
<div class="scenario-controls"><label for="scenario">Choose an experiment</label><select id="scenario" disabled><option>Loading recorded runs…</option></select><div class="presets"><button data-scenario="duplicate" disabled>01 Duplicate</button><button data-scenario="quarantine" disabled>02 Bad record</button><button data-scenario="recovery" disabled>03 Crash & recover</button><button data-scenario="replay" disabled>04 Replay</button></div></div>
<div class="lab-grid"><div class="machine-card iso" data-theme="dark"><div class="figure-top"><span>FIG. 01</span><span>EVENT INSPECTION / RECEIPT PRESS</span></div><div class="iso-stage"><!-- MACHINE --></div><div class="figure-bottom"><span>RED PARCEL = SELECTED EVENT</span><span id="outcome">READY / UNCOMMITTED</span></div></div><aside class="readouts"><p class="eyebrow">COMMITTED SINK STATE</p><dl><div><dt>Checkpoint</dt><dd id="checkpoint">0</dd></div><div><dt>Active orders</dt><dd id="active_orders">0</dd></div><div><dt>Quarantined</dt><dd id="quarantine_count">0</dd></div><div><dt>Paid total · synthetic</dt><dd id="paid_cents">$0.00</dd></div><div><dt>Durable receipts</dt><dd id="receipt_count">0</dd></div></dl><p class="small">The source sequence tracks consumption. The entity version protects the latest order state. They are different counters.</p></aside></div>
<div class="playback"><button id="play" disabled>Run experiment ▶</button><button id="step" disabled>Next step →</button><button id="reset" disabled>Reset ↺</button><span id="progress">Recorded run unavailable until data loads.</span></div><div class="narrative" role="status" aria-live="polite"><p class="eyebrow" id="event-meta">SOURCE → INSPECTION → COMMITTED STATE</p><h3 id="scenario-title">Recorded experiments</h3><p id="explanation">Use the runnable Python experiment below to reproduce the database results. This illustration is a teaching metaphor; it is not a live backend.</p></div><details><summary>Inspect the recorded event history</summary><ol id="history"><li>Run the Python recorder to inspect all transitions and evidence.</li></ol></details><noscript><p>JavaScript is disabled. The static machine remains visible. Read the case study and JSON evidence below, or run the Python scenarios locally.</p></noscript>
</section>
<section class="engineering"><p class="eyebrow">03 / UNDER THE SURFACE</p><h2>The animation explains it.<br>The transactions prove it.</h2><div class="columns"><article><span class="number">01</span><h3>Write together.</h3><p>An order change and its outbox event share a source transaction. A crash cannot commit one without the other.</p></article><article><span class="number">02</span><h3>Commit together.</h3><p>The projection, receipt, quarantine result and checkpoint share one sink transaction. An injected crash rolls them back.</p></article><article><span class="number">03</span><h3>Replay safely.</h3><p>Envelope identity detects exact replays. Entity versions and delete tombstones prevent stale updates from changing current state.</p></article></div><div class="architecture" aria-label="Architecture">Order command → Source SQLite: order + outbox<br>Ordered poll → Sink SQLite: state + receipt + checkpoint<br>SQL snapshots → Recorded JSON → This interactive replay</div><p class="small">Single-host SQLite demonstration, built on LedgerStream. No Kafka or cloud deployment; no exactly-once claim across external services. Invalid payload and stale-version scenarios use explicitly labeled transport fixtures.</p></section>
<section class="reproduce"><p class="eyebrow">04 / CHECK THE WORK</p><h2>Don't take the animation's word for it.</h2><p>Clone the repository, then run from its root. Python 3.11+; no cloud credentials required.</p><pre><code>python3 scripts/verify_signalworks.py
python3 -m signalworks
python3 -m http.server 8000
# Open /demos/signalworks/</code></pre><div class="links"><a href="../../docs/signalworks.md">Read case study ↗</a><a href="../../evidence/signalworks-traces.json">Inspect recorded evidence ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/Kartikeya-Rana-2004/engineering-portfolio">View source ↗</a></div></section>
